Z||000000||Eric_PA||08-30-2001||06:51 AM||||Has anyone tried converting a non Fiero Getrag over using Rodneys parts? I am a bit confused as to what is all involved with this. Do I need a new slave cylinder(A Fiero one) or could I use the non Fiero slave with its bracket and just convert the hydraulic line over. I have a Fiero Getrag and a Beretta Getrag on hand, but both will require linkage to use, so I would rather just convert using a FWD trans so they are easier to ind if I blow one out. Any info would be appreciated.<P>I forgot to mention that this is for a 3800 conversion and the speedo sending unit from the FWD Getrag is more desireable.<P>Thanks,<BR>Eric <p>[This message has been edited by Eric_PA (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||08-30-2001||08:19 AM||||i did it in my GT last year.  the only thing that you use off of the berreta/corsica tranny is the insides and housing.  you will need to replace the shifter select brackets, the slave cylinder bracket, and cylinder.  <P>thats all i can think of at the moment (sense you don't need to replace the pick up sensor).<P>rodney is pretty clear about the things you need to replace.<BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodney||08-30-2001||10:40 AM||||All the info you need should be here:<P>   <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/getraginfo.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/getraginfo.htm</A> <BR>   (Getrag conversion articale)<P>   <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/n36.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/n36.html</A> <BR>   (split the case info)<P>||||reg||1
